  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Middle route – breakout through the centre and a finish",
  "description": "Full court, goalkeeper in the goal the team attacks. Two defenders, A and B, stand in their own zone level with the crease, one on each side, and A has the ball. The centre C stands just over the centre line and the forward D in front of goal in the attacking zone. The rest wait in a line behind their own goal.\n\nC comes back into their own half and gets the pass from A. At the same time B moves up along the boards. C plays the ball out to B, who carries it up into the attacking zone. D comes towards the ball in front of goal, gets the pass from B and finishes.\n\nRotation: A becomes B, B becomes the centre, C becomes the forward and D joins the line. A new A steps in from the line. Switch sides after a few minutes. Variant: a defender in the middle zone tries to cut out the pass to the centre. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "C: come back when A is ready to pass – not too early, not too late."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "B: move up the boards in the passing lane, so C has an easy pass out."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "A breakout through the middle draws the defence in and opens the wing."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "D: come towards the ball in front of goal with the stick on the floor."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
